2. Place data — Amap (高德地图 / Autonavi)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The place library in `web/places.poi.js` (generated by `scripts/fetch_poi.py` and
`scripts/build_places.py`) and the copy inlined into `SmoothGo-Web-Demo.html`
contains records retrieved through the Amap Web JS API / Web-service API
(https://lbs.amap.com). For each place this includes, where Amap returned it:

  * name, category, address, district and coordinates;
  * telephone number (560 of 574 records carry one);
  * rating and opening hours;
  * photographs, referenced by URL from Amap content hosts
    (`store.is.autonavi.com`, `aos-comment.amap.com`) — 1,074 references in
    total. No image file is copied into this repository; every photograph is
    fetched from Amap at render time.

All rights in that data and those photographs remain with 高德软件有限公司
(Autonavi Software Co., Ltd.). They are **not** covered by the MIT License above
and are included here solely for teaching and demonstration. This repository is
not affiliated with, endorsed by, or licensed by Autonavi; use of the data is
subject to the Amap open-platform terms of service and quota limits
(https://lbs.amap.com/pages/terms). Commercial redistribution is not permitted
by this notice.

If you are a rights holder and want any item removed, open an issue in this
repository or use GitHub's "Report content" flow on the repository page; the
affected records will be deleted and regenerated. Regeneration is cheap — the
library is rebuilt from `scripts/fetch_poi.py` against your own Amap key.

Map rendering, route planning (`AMap.Driving` / `Transfer` / `Walking`), the live
traffic overlay (`AMap.TileLayer.Traffic`), POI search and geolocation are all
Amap services, used under the same terms. Running the app requires an Amap Web JS
API key that you apply for yourself; none is distributed here.

